I would say that a sentence containing {xu} is a question, and you=20
intended the main clause to be an assertion, so {xu} isn't what you=20
want.

> I mean, {goi} is =85 performative? =85 so
> I should not ask about truth values (which is what {xu} is for?) but
> about =85 appropriateness?

Yes, {goi} is performative. I probably wouldn't use {goi} in this=20
sentence at all. I would use {no'u} or {noi}, or {to ... toi}.

> Would {pei} have been better?

It clashes a little bit with the {goi}; "hereby the same as X, how do=20
you feel about that?". It might be better than {xu}, although it's not=20
entirely clear if {pei} causes irrealis or not. I could see it going=20
either way.

You could say:

      (1) la re moi nunji'e (to xu du la'o gy. Second Life .gy toi)

or if you want to use your {pei} idea, provided that it doesn't affect=20
the mood:

      (2) la re moi nunji'e ku no'u pei la'o gy. Second Life .gy

(note that you forgot a {ku})

I would most likely go with (1), personally. The {pei} feels a bit=20
weird to me.

